diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..7f0f933 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,24 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Page transitions
+
+The shared layout uses native cross-document view transitions. Unsupported browsers
+use ordinary navigation, and reduced-motion preferences disable the animation.
+The global stylesheet is emitted in the head, and the masthead font stylesheet is
+render-blocking. `rel="expect"` waits for `#masthead` and a page's opening content
+(`transitionReadyId`, defaulting to `page-intro`), without waiting for the footer,
+ads, analytics, or the article body. New pages must include their matching target.
+
+There is currently no theme or layout bootstrap script. If one is added, put it in
+the shared head or the layout's `head` slot and mark it `blocking="render"` (and
+`is:inline` for Astro to preserve the script attributes). Keep it small; never
+apply render blocking to third-party analytics or ad loaders.
+
+Readiness targets guarantee parsed HTML, not downloaded image pixels. Opening
+story images load eagerly with high fetch priority and explicit dimensions to
+preserve their layout while loading.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
